  "notes": "Throughput tracks the actual L(G) edge yield, not just |E(G)|. Sparse path inputs run at ~16 Melem/s of input (≈|E(L)| ≈ |E(G)| so this is also ~16 Melem/s of output). Dense K_n inputs are dominated by the n^4 output: K_64 inputs ~2016 edges but emits ~125k L-edges in ~6.2 ms (~20 M L-edges/s). Star inputs are the worst case per input edge — n^2/2 L-edges per (n−1) inputs — yet star/2048 still finishes in ~88 ms (~24 M L-edges/s of output). Directed chains hit ~26 M input arcs/s consistently across 3 orders of magnitude, confirming the per-source incoming-walk in the directed branch is Θ(in-degree) per emitted L-arc — chain inputs have in/out degree 1, so only 1 L-arc per input. ER G(n,m) at n=2048, m=8192 finishes in ~2.6 ms which is ~3.2 M input edges/s; here the realistic mixed-degree case averages ~5 L-edges per input edge so it sits between the path and K_n extremes."
